PER-ARM ORACLES: tests validating ONE arm against its own semantics
  quantiser-fadd-shared          ['software_add_matches_hardware_bit_exact']
  quantiser-radix-shared         ['radix_ten_delivers_the_nearest_grid_point_ties_to_even', 'radix_two_instantiation_matches_the_silicon']

THE DECLARATION MISMATCH
  A family classified PROPERTY-PINNING ONLY whose bridge declares
  outputs_may_differ = false is telling the harness its arms must
  agree byte-for-byte while its own validator does not require it.
    quantiser-fadd-shared          PROPERTY-PINNING ONLY  with outputs_may_differ false (default)
    quantiser-radix-shared         PROPERTY-PINNING ONLY  with outputs_may_differ false (default)

READING
  ANSWER-PINNING is the only classification that supports the claim
  that a family's numbers compare cost at a fixed answer. A family
  that pins only a property admits arms computing different values,
  and whether they do is a separate measurement (p2, p3, p4).
